                    <p>Copper Phthalocyanine Blue Pigment, also known as Pigment Blue 15 (PB15), is a vibrant and widely recognized blue pigment known for its brilliant shade, excellent fastness properties, and exceptional stability. It belongs to the phthalocyanine family and is synthesized through the complex reaction of phthalic anhydride, urea, copper salt, and catalysts.</p>
                    <p>The pigment is available in multiple forms based on its crystalline structure and tone — including Alpha (PB 15:0 to PB 15:2) and Beta (PB 15:3 to PB 15:4) — offering a wide spectrum of bluish tones from red-shade blue to green-shade blue.</p>
                    <p>This pigment has become a staple in multiple industries due to its superior performance in terms of color retention, heat resistance, dispersibility, and environmental safety.</p>
